00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:04.130 align:start position:0%
Rainbow six siege has just received the  third of its for Plan B 1 dlc packs  operation scale rain the Brazilian theme  DLC adds two new operators attacker  Kappa Tau and defender kuvira a new map  favela that features exterior shell  destruction a tactical realism custom  game mode as well as a bunch of minor  fixes I spent pretty much a full day  diving into the new content so let me  give you the rundown on what I found the  new favela map like all previously  released maps is free for all players  much has been made of the new exterior  shell destruction which allows players  to blow out exterior walls to minimize  hiding places for the opposing team  these walls are all destructible by all  the usual means sledge ash thermite  breaching charges and good old elbow  grease the objective sights on favela  have plenty of destructible walls so  camping in an unreinforced corner isn't  the best idea roaming seems to be the  way to go for this map as it's easy to  get the drop on your opponents in the  maze like layout speaking of getting the  drop on opponents the first new operator  kuvira is a dynamo for roaming and  sneaking her first unique ability is  silent step that allows her to get up  close without alerting enemies in order  to incapacitate and interrogate them  revealing enemy positions on the map  when using silent step Guevera is  restricted to a sidearm Louis son a  non-lethal pistol with a built-in  silencer I'm garbage with side arms  which is why I never play shield  operators so I never really used silent  step to its full potential that being  said in the right hands being able to  down enemies and then interrogate them  will be invaluable and when paired with  frost swell compatibility interrogation  is going to be an absolute beast as it  stands now I'm not sure where I sit on  the interrogation ability I've always  liked the tagging enemies with drones  and cameras gives you a static position  marker that doesn't follow the enemy but  interrogation marks enemies with their  operators symbol and it follows them for  about 10 seconds it's kind of like when  it defender ventures outside part of me  feels that 10 seconds is too long while  the other things that it's a worthy  reward for the risk of exposing yourself  for the time it takes to execute the  interrogation it's going to be  interesting to see how the community and  players far above my skill level and  double using Povera the second new  operator is the attacker capital his  unique ability is a micro crossbow that  fires two different kinds of ammunition  the first a micro smoke grenades that  can be deployed to cover your advance  well the second area of effect is  fixating bolts basically they're flaming  arrows to burn off the oxygen in a small  area damaging enemies in close proximity  they're grateful when you need to keep  an enemy from advancing  when you want to flush someone out of a  hiding place you can't quite get an  angle on hot tip no pun intended  asphyxiating bolts are deadly to Kappa  Tau so don't make the same mistake I did  by firing them into the wall in front of  you the micro smoke grenades I found  useful at least in theory as  misdirection I tried to fly them over  the head of enemies to try and make it  seemed we were entering from a different  direction but like every round of siege  I've ever played my best laid plans  would go out the window as soon as I  encountered even the slightest hitch  usually in the form of someone shooting  me in the head unfortunately I wasn't  able to get enough people together to be  able to try the tactical realism mode  but it looks like everything I'm looking  for and more the hardcore modes goal is  to increase immersion by reducing  reliance on in-game feedback staples  like crosshairs enemy marking friendly  fire markers and kill confirmations are  all gone and there's new more realistic  magazine management there have also been  a host of tweaks and changes to the  underlying game the Ubisoft is referring  to as the health program one of the  major updates is in your attachment the  angled grip that allows faster aiming  down sights don't worry it's not call of  duty level of snappiness but I did find  it useful when I needed to draw on an  enemy in a 1v1 situation the downside is  an increased recoil so using this with  sustained fire isn't ideal but as a  burst grip for players new to siege who  may grapple with the slower pacing or  seasoned vets who like to roam around  the map it's a great addition another  handy new feature is the ability to  check what loadouts your teammates have  selected during the ready up phase a few  times I noticed we were all loading in  with barbed wire or frags so I would  back out and adjust my loadout  accordingly I also used it to check the  load out of skilled players that was  match made with so I could see how their  gear differed customizing gear is now  much prettier thanks to a full screen  weapon preview that can be zoomed to  highlight specific attachments the  tactical map has also been improved with  more detail for both defenders and  attackers the heads-up display has also  been updated with armor no longer  displayed and you player icons that  according to OB soft make determining  the status of your teammates are much  smoother process during play however I  found them you ? player indicators  harder to read the red X that denotes a  dead player has been dimmed so at a  glance it's harder to quickly identify  how many enemies are still kicking  around maybe it's just a transitional  thing I'll adjust to in time but I'd  suggest a brighter red X to make info  like this more easily read at a glance  overall operation scale rain is a  welcome improvement to an already great  lying game the addition of the two new  operators is exciting and I can't wait  to see how they end up being used in  higher skilled play the amount of  destruction on favela makes for a more  dynamic changing map that asks players  to adjust their play style and the  worker be soft is put into improving the  base game for the health program will  help maintain an audience of tactical  multiplayer shooter fans if you want to  talk Rainbow six or just video games in  general come find me on Twitter and for  a full list of the other tweaks and  changes they've been rolled out to siege  check out our coverage on gamespot
 

